TASK: Implement DuckDBFileCompareNodeOperator, Phase 2. Phase 1 is merged; build on it, do not restructure it.

SPEC: docs/specs/duckdb-file-compare.md. Relevant sections: 3 (field table, Config validation), 5.8, 5.13, 6, 7, 9, 10, Appendix A.
Where the spec differs from existing code conventions, follow the existing code and note it in the PR.

IN SCOPE (Phase 2)
1. date rule (sec 6): new RuleRenderer bean. formatLeft / formatRight optional;
   try_strptime(c::VARCHAR, fmt)::DATE on each side, try_cast(c AS DATE) when no format.
   Unparseable value = mismatch (via the existing coalesce(..., false) wrapper).
   Add its validation: blank formats rejected in stage 1; formats probed on a 1,000-row sample in stage 2
   (sec 3, Config validation).
2. thresholds.abortCandidatePct (sec 5.8, 7): candidates / keys on both sides * 100, checked right after
   pass 1. On breach: skip pass 2 and diffs, write summary.json with counts from pass 1 and a clear reason,
   status FAILED. Unset = not checked.
3. dryRun (sec 3, 9): run bind, work schema, ingest views, staging views and schema check (DESCRIBE only),
   log every generated SQL statement at INFO, read no full data, write no output files except
   summary.json with schema findings, return SUCCESS (or FAILED if schema policy fails).
4. Duplicates output file (sec 7): write dup_keys to output.duplicates when non-empty; null-key counts
   stay in summary.json.
5. Scale benchmark (sec 5.13, 10): a test or small tool, excluded from the default CI run (tag or profile),
   that generates a synthetic pair with DuckDB itself: range(20000000) rows, 2 key columns, 500 value
   columns of mixed types (VARCHAR, BIGINT, DECIMAL, DATE), right side with about 1% of rows altered,
   0.1% left-only and 0.1% right-only. Write left as CSV (several files in one directory) and right as
   Parquet. Run the operator and record per-phase timings, peak temp-dir disk use and the summary counts.
6. Tuning from the benchmark (sec 5.13): apply what the numbers show inside the job (for example explicit
   CSV types). DuckDB setup values (threads, memory, temp dir, storage) are NOT set by the job; report
   recommended values for Appendix A in the PR. Do not change the two-pass design or the output contract
   without explaining why in the PR.
7. Benchmark-driven decisions (sec 5.13, "To decide by benchmark"): on the synthetic pair, measure and
   report (a) Parquet on both sides: materialise into tables vs re-reading the files in pass 2;
   (b) pass 1 spill: if it spills heavily, try the key-bucket fallback (hash(keys) % N buckets,
   pass 1 + pass 2 per bucket); (c) typeMode text vs native for the CSV side.
   Implement materialise: auto ONLY if (a) shows a clear win, and build bucketing ONLY if (b) shows it
   is needed; justify both with the numbers. Also report which DuckDB storage setup (file-backed vs
   in-memory with spill) was fastest, as advice for Appendix A, with no code change.

OUT OF SCOPE
- keyless mode, profiling, HTML report, includeMatched (Phase 3).
- Any regex rule type (removed from the spec).
- DuckDB connection setup and settings (owned by the existing setup).

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
A. date rule tests: same date in different formats matches; different dates mismatch; unparseable
   mismatches; NULL handling with both nullEqualsNull values; blank format rejected at bind;
   wrong format caught by the stage 2 sample probe.
B. Golden tests: abortCandidatePct breached (pass 2 skipped, reason in summary) and not breached;
   dryRun (no data files written, SQL logged, schema findings in summary); duplicates file written.
C. Benchmark report in the PR: machine or pod size, DuckDB settings in effect, wall time per phase,
   peak temp disk, candidate count vs mismatched count. The counts must equal the injected changes.
   Include the three comparisons from item 7 as a small table with wall time and peak disk for each.
D. Phase 1 tests still pass unchanged (snapshot updates only where a new feature changes SQL, explained).
